      "content": "that's risky though. if a reporter brings up the specific bill number or the actual text from the record, which shows it was $2 million short and not some massive debt issue, we're dead. they'll call us liars. \n\nis there a way to spin it where we aren't technically lying about the bill content, but we can still imply it was a 'bad version' to get them off the scent? like, can we say he was waiting for a better version even though he knew that wasn't happening?",
